/*
  =====================================================================
   MACHINE MONITOR - UNIVERSAL FIRMWARE  v2.0.0
   ESP32 + W5500 LAN + NJK-5002C sensor + LM2596
  =====================================================================
   ONE .bin FOR EVERY MACHINE
   - No Device ID, key, MAC or IP is written in this code.
   - Every board has its own HW ID (factory MAC of the ESP32 chip).
   - Settings are kept in flash (NVS) and come from:
       * the SERVER  : device ID, key, counting / filter / timing settings
       * the SERIAL  : network (IP / gateway / mask / DNS / server address)
   - OTA: the same .bin is pushed to all boards from the app.

   HOW A NEW BOARD JOINS (zero code change)
   1. Set network once by USB Serial (only if the LAN has no DHCP):
        set ip 10.5.16.31
        set gw 10.5.16.254
        set mask 255.255.255.0
        set dns 10.5.16.254
        set dhcp off
        set server 10.5.20.2:5000
        reboot
   2. Board calls  POST /api/device/hello  every 30 s with its HW ID.
      The app shows it in Device Manager -> "Pending devices".
   3. In the app: Approve -> give Device ID (MC07) -> link to a machine.
   4. Next hello returns device_id + device_key + settings.
      The board saves them and starts sending events. Done.
   Replace a broken board: approve the new HW ID on the same machine.

   EVENTS (unchanged from v1.2.x, plus a few new fields)
   - Board ONLY counts pulses. App turns them into courses and pieces.
   - RUNNING / IDLE (no pulse for idle_timeout_ms) / COUNT (every
     send_every_pulses) / HEARTBEAT / SCHEDULED / RESET / BOOT
   - Queue of 64 events when the network or server is down.

   REMOTE CONTROL FROM THE APP
   - Settings: the server sends cfg_ver; if it differs, the board downloads
     GET /api/device/config and saves the new settings.
   - Commands: reset_count, reboot, ota_check, clear_stats, lan_rescan
     (each runs once; the board reports it back as cmd_ack).

   SAFETY
   - Task watchdog: board restarts itself if the program hangs > 30 s.
   - Pulse counting runs in its own 1 ms timer (noise filter from v1.2.1).

   !! Keep the OTA code in every new version and raise FW_VERSION.
   !! Partition Scheme: "Minimal SPIFFS (1.9MB APP with OTA)"

   WIRING (same as before)
     W5500: 5V->5V/VIN, GND, MISO->19, MOSI->23, SCLK->18, SCS->5, RST->4
     Sensor: signal -> GPIO27 (4.7k pull-up to 3.3V or PC817 output)

   LIBRARY: "Ethernet" by Arduino
   SERIAL 115200 (Serial Monitor: "Newline"):
     i  status          show  settings      register  ask server now
     c  simulate pulse  s     heartbeat     r  reset count
     d  clear filter stats    u  OTA check  n / f  LAN mode next / auto
     set id <ID> | set key <KEY> | set ip/gw/mask/dns <a.b.c.d>
     set dhcp on|off | set server <a.b.c.d[:port]> | set mac <AA:..>|auto
     set wifi <ssid> <pass> | set wifi off | reboot | factory
  =====================================================================
*/

